course: dictionary
lesson: 3509
title: Serious words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hard word often has clues in the sentences around it. In «There were no fatalities in the crash», the word no tells you the answer is zero, and crash tells you something went wrong on the road. Fatalities must be about deaths, so the sentence means nobody died.
explain: Fatality is a serious, formal word. You will find it in news reports and safety lessons, where writers use it to count deaths quickly and plainly. «Road fatalities» means people who died in road accidents.
explain: Leo says he has «seen all the fatalities already, they're nothing», but then he watches through his fingers with his eyes shut. His actions give the clue. Someone who is truly unbothered does not hide. Leo's words sound tough, but he is scared. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: A fatality is a death caused by an accident, war, disaster or violence.
fact: «Fatalities» is the plural, which means more than one death.
fact: «No fatalities» means nobody died.
fact: Fatality can also mean the quality of causing death, as in «the fatality of the disease».
fact: In geography, reports about earthquakes, floods and storms often count the fatalities.
exercise: «There were no fatalities in the crash.» What does fatalities mean? | Injuries to the car | Driving lessons | *Deaths | Police officers
exercise: The report counted the road fatalities. What does road fatalities mean? | Roads that were built last year | Traffic lights that stopped working | Cars for sale on the road | *People who died in road accidents
exercise: Leo says he has seen all the fatalities already, but he watches through his fingers. What does his behaviour suggest? | He is completely calm and bored | *He is pretending to be brave | He loves horror films | He is fast asleep
test: «The flood caused three fatalities.» How many people died? | None | *Three | Ten cars | Thirty
test: In a formal report, what does fatality mean? | A happy event for the whole town | A kind of weather | A new road built by the council | *A death caused by an accident, war, disaster or violence
exam: What does «no fatalities» tell the reader? | Lots of people were hurt | The storm was very big | *Nobody died | Everyone was rescued
